{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"title":"Choosing what to record","generated":true,"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What it calls","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FileManager.fileExists","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Data.write(to:options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"FileVersionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"ProcessInfo.perform